===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|taxen}}, from {{der|en|xno|taxer||to impose a tax}}, from {{der|en|la|taxāre}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|taxō||I handle”, “I censure”, “I appraise”, “I compute}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To impose and collect a tax from (a person or company).
#: {{ux|en|Some think to '''tax''' the wealthy is the fairest.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Formerly known as food|author=Kristin Lawless|year=2018|ISBN=9781250078315|page=251
|passage='''Taxing''' the food and chemical industries, which make billions off our food consumption, could be another way to generate revenue for the program.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To impose and collect a tax on (something).
#: {{ux|en|Some think to '''tax''' wealth is destructive of a private sector.}}
# {{senseid|en|overdemand}}{{lb|en|transitive}} To make excessive demands on.
#: {{ux|en|Do not '''tax''' my patience.}}
#* {{RQ:Melville Omoo
|passage=The people of the southeasterly clusters—concerning whom, however, but little is known—have a bad name as cannibals; and for that reason their hospitality is seldom '''taxed''' by the mariner.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1960|month=February|author=R. C. Riley|title=The London-Birmingham services - Past, Present and Future|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=103|text=The heavy freight traffic which shares the double line between [[Paddington]] and [[Wolverhampton]] with the passenger traffic has '''taxed''' the ingenuity of the timetable planners.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2007 January 16|title=IBM - Reinventing the invention system - United States|journal=IDEAS from IBM|url=http://www.ibm.com/ibm/ideasfromibm/us/patents/011607/images/IFI_01162007.pdf|passage=But patent applications are increasingly accompanied by volumes and volumes of data on DVD, which '''taxes''' the resources of the patent office.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[accuse]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[examine]] accounts in order to allow or disallow items.

